.TH DRAGONGL_SERVER 1 "2026-09-06" "DragonGL 2026.09.04.02" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl_server \- Dragon GL master game server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl_server
.RI "[\-\-password\ |\ -p\ " pwd ]"
.RI "[\-\-dm\-password\ |\ -d\ " pwd ]"
.RI "[\-\-port\ |\ -P\ " port ]"
.RI "[\-\-data\-dir\ |\ -D\ " dir ]"
.RI "[\-\-help\ |\ -h ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl_server
is the authoritative server of the Dragon GL client/server dungeon crawler.
It generates and maintains the master world (a 300x300 dungeon spanning
101 floors), runs monster AI, resolves combat, and synchronizes the game
state with all connected clients over TCP.

The server listens on port
.BR 8080
(unless changed with
.BR \-\-port ).

Security notes:
.IP \- 2
Usernames are restricted to
.BR 1-16
alphanumeric/underscore characters (they are used to build file names).
.IP \- 2
The privileged
.B dm
account requires a
.I dedicated
password (
.BR \-\-dm-password ): knowing the plain server access password
no longer grants DM powers (dm_spawn, dm_goto, dm_pdf, ...).
.IP \- 2
Passwords are stored salted (FNV-1a, salt derived from the username).
The protocol is NOT encrypted: passwords travel in clear over TCP, which
is acceptable on a trusted LAN but should not be exposed to the Internet.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-password " pwd"
Set the password required by clients to join the server.
Default:
.I dragongl_secret
(a warning is printed at boot while the default is in use).
.TP
.BI \-d ", " \-\-dm-password " pwd"
Set the password of the dedicated
.B dm
account.
Default:
.IR dragongl_dm_secret .
.TP
.BI \-P ", " \-\-port " port"
TCP port to listen on (default 8080). Useful to run several servers on
the same machine or to test in parallel.
.TP
.BI \-D ", " \-\-data-dir " dir"
Directory holding the JSON datasets and the world state files
(world.dat, npcs.dat, artifacts.dat).
When not given, the server uses
.IR ./data
if it contains
.IR bestiary.json ,
otherwise
.IR /usr/share/dragongl/data
(RPM install).
.TP
.B \-h , \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I combat_log.json
Tactical combat log, written in the working directory.
.TP
.IR saves/ "directory"
Player save files (*.save) and tombstones (tombstone_*.dat).
.TP
.IR data/ "directory"
World persistence files (world.dat, artifacts.dat, npcs.dat).
world.dat carries a magic/version/CRC32 header (1 byte per tile, the
volatile entity grid is not persisted); a missing or invalid file is
never half-loaded — the server generates a fresh world instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl_client (1),
.BR dragongl-server (1),
.BR dragongl_reset_world (1)
